	I once toyed with the idea of a Conservation of Rockery patch.
Thinking as I type:

   o  Make statues weigh 2.7 times as much as the monster.  (Most
      common rocks have a density of ~2.7.)

   o  Have minimum statue weights of 100 * monster size**2, to keep
      statues of air elementals from being weightless and eggshell-
      thin.

   o  When shattering a statue, you get 50-99% of the statue's weight
      back as rocks.  (You lose some as gravel and sand.)  So, smashing
      a boulder gives back 50-99% of 6000/10, or 300 to 594 rocks.  
      A dragon statue gives, what, 100+?  And the statues in the early
      game give back few or no rocks.

   o  Broken rocks weigh 10.  Change the weight of meatballs from 1
      to 10/2.7 = 4.  Change the nutrition from 5 to 20.

   o  Change the weight of huge chunks of meat from 400 to 6000/2.7
      = 2200.  Change the nutrition from 2000 to 11000.

   o  Change the nutrition of statues from 900 to 5 * statue weight.

	The main change to game balance would be for healers in the
early game.  A heap of rocks in the mines would give four times as 
much nutrition as now.  If they manage to break a statue, they 
probably get less nutrition than now (since they'll get back few or 
no rocks for small, low-level monsters).  If they manage to break a
boulder, their food worries are over:  they get the equivalent of 7
to 15 food rations.  (Eight times heavier, yes, but still:  lotsa
food.)  Overall, early-game healers are easier.

	I don't want to lower the nutrition-to-weight ratios of 
meatballs and chunks of meat, since the current ratio of 5 is already
wretchedly low.

	We could say that stone-to-flesh only works on the first
Clev * 100 (?) weights of rock.  (Make partially S-to-F-ing an object
give 100% success, so it always works on at least one statue.)  I'm
afraid that I'm unenthused about having such an obvious kludge to 
work around a YANI's flaw.


	So, it makes the game more consistent (good) but easier (bad).
To me, it looks like an even match.  Unless you feel otherwise (or
can suggest a better fix), I think I'll kick this YANI off the edge
of the world.

